\f2\b \cf7 \cb8 ## Step-by-Step: What Each Command Does
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
\

\f2\b \cf7 \cb8 ### 1. Get an API Key
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
Go to [NVIDIA API Catalog](https://build.nvidia.com) \uc0\u8594  Sign up \u8594  Generate API Key\
\
This key proves you're allowed to download NVIDIA's containers.\
\

\f2\b \cf7 \cb8 ### 2. Login to NVIDIA's Container Registry
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \

\f2\b \cf10 \cb8 bash
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 docker login nvcr.io\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 # Username: $oauthtoken  (type this literally)\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 # Password: <paste your API key>\cf9 \cb8 \
\
This is like logging into a private app store to download the NIM container.\
\

\f2\b \cf7 \cb8 ### 3. Set Environment Variables
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \

\f2\b \cf10 \cb8 bash
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 export NGC_API_KEY=<your_key>        # Your API key\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 export LOCAL_NIM_CACHE=~/.cache/nim  # Where to store downloaded models\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 mkdir -p "$LOCAL_NIM_CACHE"          # Create that folder\cf9 \cb8 \
\
\

\f2\b \cf7 \cb8 ### 4. Run the Container
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \

\f2\b \cf10 \cb8 bash
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 docker run -it --rm \\\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     --gpus all \\              # Give container access to your GPU(s)\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     --shm-size=16GB \\         # Shared memory for multi-GPU communication\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     -e NGC_API_KEY \\          # Pass your API key inside\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     -v "$LOCAL_NIM_CACHE:/opt/nim/.cache" \\  # Save models locally\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     -p 8000:8000 \\            # Expose port 8000 for API calls\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     nvcr.io/nim/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct:latest\cf9 \cb8 \
\
\

\f2\b \cf10 \cb8 What each flag means:
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
| Flag | Purpose |\
|------|---------|\
| \cf11 \cb8 --gpus all\cf9 \cb8  | Let container use your NVIDIA GPU |\
| \cf11 \cb8 --shm-size=16GB\cf9 \cb8  | Memory for GPU communication |\
| \cf11 \cb8 -e NGC_API_KEY\cf9 \cb8  | Authentication to download models |\
| \cf11 \cb8 -v ...:/opt/nim/.cache\cf9 \cb8  | Don't re-download models every time |\
| \cf11 \cb8 -p 8000:8000\cf9 \cb8  | Make API accessible at localhost:8000 |\
\

\f2\b \cf7 \cb8 ### 5. Test It
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \

\f2\b \cf10 \cb8 bash
\f3\b0 \cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8 curl -X POST 'http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions' \\\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8   -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8   -d '\{\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     "model": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct",\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8     "messages": [\{"role":"user", "content":"Hello!"\}]\cf9 \cb8 \
\cf11 \cb8   \}'\cf9 \cb8 \
\
